{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_3dclw42h225wdpm23f7clcdu55wabzm4ibtbfolm6lv4mp22ryjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## Scope enumerated\nThe whole library is `c_src/src/lib.c` (181 lines) + `c_src/include/lib.h`, built by CMake as one shared lib. `nm -D` on the C `.so` exports **9** symbols — no namespace/renaming macros in the header, so linker names equal source names.\n\n## Symbol diff: empty\n| C `.so` | Rust `.so` |\n|---|---|\n| apply_bitmask, arity, arity2, arity3, arity4, compare_allocations, init_matrix, process_string, shift_array | identical 9 `T` symbols |\n\n`comm -23 c.syms r.syms` → nothing missing.\n\n## Behavioral verification (byte-identical)\nBuilt a `dlopen` driver that exercises all 9 exports and ran it once per `.so`:\n- Structured sweep: 11,549 lines — **same md5** (`de4ead52…`) for C and Rust.\n- Randomized fuzz: 60,000 mixed calls, 937,378 bytes — `cmp` clean.\n\n## Faithfulness details preserved (not \"fixed\")\n- **`arity` prototype mismatch:** the header declares `int arity(int, int*)` but the definition takes `unsigned char len`. Disassembly confirms gcc truncates `%edi` to `%al`, so `len=256` → `0` → returns `-1`. Rust takes `c_int` and masks `& 0xFF`, reproducing this exactly (declaring `u8` in Rust would emit `zeroext`, which would *not* truncate a C caller's wide value).\n- **`compare_allocations` address comparison:** the result depends on real allocator behavior — because both pointers are freed each call, glibc's tcache LIFO makes consecutive calls alternate between `1` and `2`. Rust calls libc `malloc`/`free` directly (not Rust's allocator wrapper) so this ordering matches; the `uninit_ptr` read (`*ptr1 == val1`) adds `10` when `val1 > 0`.\n- **`process_string`** dereferences its argument with no NULL check — reproduced.\n- **`shift_array`** silently no-ops unless `0 < positions < size`; overlapping copy uses `ptr::copy` (memmove).\n- **`param1 % 4`** keeps C's truncate-toward-zero remainder, so negative inputs yield `-1/-2/-3` and fall through `apply_bitmask`'s `default` branch unchanged.\n- Signed overflow in `result * param3` / the accumulations uses `wrapping_*` to match gcc `-O0` two's-complement behavior instead of panicking.\n\n`Cargo.toml` uses `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`; all exports are `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`. `cargo build --release` succeeds with no warnings, and nothing in `c_src/` was modified (mtimes unchanged)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":944,"cache_read_input_tokens":35996,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":944,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0fac23a0-278c-468b-b2cf-b02a0b963f33","uuid":"3e62ac59-3267-45ea-ad72-5c8b1570978d","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:01:49.221Z"}
